  "quality_gate": [
    "Only Phase 14 source_inventory_complete municipalities may enter the Phase 15 record-review queue.",
    "Every promoted record must retain an official source URL and a record-level evidence locator such as page, table, section, paragraph, row, or stable HTML locator.",
    "Current plan identity, implementation layer, annual progress or evaluation, budget state, settlement state, audit, assembly, and accountability roles must remain distinct whenever the official source distinguishes them.",
    "Proposal, enacted budget, supplementary budget, execution, settlement, project cost, contract amount, subsidy amount, and other fiscal values must never be collapsed into one undifferentiated number.",
    "Plan version, target year, measurement year, reporting year, fiscal year, publication year, evaluation year, and source retrieval state must remain separate fields when the source distinguishes them.",
    "Source-reported evaluations, committee findings, citizen surveys, and administrative assessments may be preserved as attributed source facts but must not become independent Jichi Insight achievement judgments.",
    "Historical or prior-plan evidence must not be reused as current-plan actuals unless an official source explicitly establishes the linkage and the version boundary is preserved.",
    "Draft, transition, not-yet-published, unresolved, rounded, aggregate-only, and unavailable evidence states remain explicit and may block individual records without downgrading already verified Source Inventory coverage.",
    "No causal attribution, cross-city comparison eligibility, composite score, ranking, or political evaluation may be promoted during Phase 15 without a separate comparability and methodology review.",
    "A municipality is not Phase 15 reviewed_complete until its declared review package passes schema validation, official-source evidence coverage checks, non-inference gates, regression tests, and final repository/web/production verification."
  ],
